Z||000003||JohnnyK||02-09-2001||12:51 AM||||What? Why are the steering columns different?||||reg||1
Z||000004||Indiana_resto_guy||02-09-2001||01:51 AM||||The only difference btwn the two is that the manual has a 'key lock release' lever.<BR>The column may be installed in either and will still work properly!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Rodney||02-09-2001||08:56 AM||||When I changed my 88 Mera from an automatic to a 5 speed I left in the automatic steering column. It is so nice not having that key release lever to deal with!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroJoe||02-09-2001||09:34 AM||||The the key lock release lever thingy is supposed to remind me to put my car in gear or set the brake, it sure dosent work.  I have just gotten used to pushing it down as I turn the car off, I just do it without thinking.  So a lot of good that is doing.<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-09-2001||08:31 PM||||It might work but it would be a pain in the rear. You'd need to carefully move the interlock cable. You might need to use the automatic's ignition switch. Either way you can get this local cheaper that Ebay plus shipping.<P>The lock button isn't ment to remind you of anything. It's to prevent turning the key to lock while the car is running which would also lock the steering.... ||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroJoe||02-09-2001||09:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>It's to prevent turning the key to lock while the car is running which would also lock the steering....<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So why would only manual cars have these?  I have seen them on almost every GM standard transmission car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Cooter||02-09-2001||09:59 PM||||An automatic car will not allow the key to be turned all the way to lock unless it is in park.||||reg||1
Z||000010||FieroJoe||02-09-2001||10:33 PM||||Ah i see.  Havent ever tried that with my parents "newer" cars, but I was just kinda curious because my winter car, 86 volvo, doesnt have anything like that, you dont even have to have the brake depressed to take it out of park.<P>Oh well, lotsa things that are wierd with that car.  Thanks for the info!||||reg||1
